PX Core-API LuaLS Addon
======================================

This works with any editor running lua-language-server. It's built
from the addon-template. This works better than a workspace library
since multiple projects in different directories may be using the API.

  ptokax-api.lua        generated definitions, do not edit
  gen-api-defs.lua      regenerates them from scripting-interface.txt

Setup
-----

Drop wherever works for you. The hope is that the addon gets autodetected.

Then wherever it settles just add the name of the directory that contains
the pxapi-addon folder to your Lua.workspace.userThirdParty value.

For instance, if you use a .luarc.json file placed in your scripts folder
and your LusLS Addons folder is in ~/.local/share/luals/addons should be
placed in your .luarc.json. Then when opening your IDE/Editor LuaLS should
read the json file and load the addon (if the script file matches nicely.)

JSON

{
  "Lua.workspace.userThirdParty": ["/home/username/.local/share/luals/addons"]
}


See here: https://luals.github.io/wiki/addons/#addon-manager


Event functions need annotating
-------------------------------

LuaLS doesn't do parameter types from global, so tUser is
unknown until specified: 

	--- @param tUser User
	--- @param sData string
	function ChatArrival(tUser, sData)
		Core.SendToAll(tUser.sNick .. sData)
	end

Followed by <leader>pa to save. Put the cursor on the function line and it
inserts one --- @param per argument.

Generation of definitions file
------------------------------

	lua contrib/nvim/gen-api-defs.lua scripting.docs/scripting-interface.txt \
	    > contrib/nvim/lua/pxapi/ptokax-api.lua

Names the rule cannot type are in the OVERRIDE table near the top.

It's mostly obvious how the scripting-interface text corresponds to the 
terms as defined. The Hungarian Notation convention helps us along. Returns
come from the table of returns. 

Anything not listed falls back to reading the description, which gives boolean?
for "Return nil when failed, true when success" (this is wrong-ish),
table for "Return table with", and any otherwise.


Known gaps
----------

Overloads are emitted in document order, so the first form listed is the one
signature help shows first. Core.GetOnlineUsers has four. 

Functions taking sNick/sIP alternatives are typed from the first name only,
so BanMan.GetBan is string either way.

